 ## Overview
-Vector Icon Volume Rendering is a 3D raster resampling technique that integrates vector field visualization into scalar volume rendering by embedding small billboard images containing vector icons within the splat footprint of the volume rendering sheets [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of visualizing flow direction and magnitude within a volumetric scalar field (such as density clouds) by creating an illusion of coherent flow through stochastic placement and orientation of these icons [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from standard direct volume ray casting by replacing continuous integration with a discrete, stochastic sampling of vector indicators overlaid on the scalar volume, and differs from pure vector field visualization (like streamlines) by maintaining the volumetric context of the scalar data [S1, unofficial].
+Vector Icon Volume Rendering is a 3D raster resampling technique that integrates vector field visualization into scalar volume rendering by embedding small billboard images containing vector icons within the splat footprint of the volume rendering sheets [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of visualizing flow direction and magnitude within a volumetric scalar field by creating an illusion of coherent flow through stochastic placement and orientation of these icons [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from continuous integration methods by modifying the volume integral to include rendering of tiny cylinders within a small neighborhood of each sampling point, and differs from pure vector field visualization by merging the rendering of a scalar field with that of a vector field in a single compositing pass [S1, unofficial].
 
